  "summary": "York, Maine voters approved a slate of six referendum questions, including a 'Stop ALPRs' ordinance permanently banning automated license plate reading cameras by any public agency in town, passing 5,386-2,043. The York Police Department had already terminated its Flock Safety contract and removed at least four cameras in September following a citizen petition.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Residents also voted to ban automated license plate reading cameras, or ALPRs, in a 5,386-2,043 vote amid a nationwide debate over the ethics of similar technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    },
    {
      "quote": "The York Police Department terminated its contract with the ALPR company Flock Safety in September and removed at least four cameras on public property following a citizen petition that garnered 115 signatures.",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    },
    {
      "quote": "Tuesday's decision implements an ordinance permanently barring any public agency in town from using similar technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    }
